silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_yoneda_hom_leg_2 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeTsnIdentityLegForbiddenBareIdentityExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_02_probe_tsn_identity_yoneda_hom_leg_2 silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeTsnIdentityLegForbiddenBareIdentity', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, gippidy00 §1 (Mittens may factor through Felis catus / TSN 183798; Mittens may not factor through the bare string catus): equivalently for the numeric identifier, Mittens may factor through the TaxRow object, but not through the bare TSN integer. The forbidden arrow Hom(BareTsnNumeric, Mittens) is empty in O_01." .
